In article <u906438-130893152314@mathsmacla61h75.its.utas.edu.au> u906438@postoffice.utas.edu.au (Paul Saunders) writes:
>Just started up my save game on the Mac and got the following message which
>is amusing and worth sharing.
>
>"Watch Out! Bad things can happen on Friday the 13th."

It may not be that amusing - I think it lowers your luck by one when it
does that. Similar messages occur for new and full moons (lower and raise
luck respectively).

Actually, it occurred to me at the last full moon (when I was still playing
this silly game ;) that this is open to mild abuse. It seems to increment
your luck each time you restart a saved game on a full moon day; one could
save and restart the game 10 times or so, and start out with a really choice
luck score. Even better to do it after finding a luckstone. Alternately,
someone who saves and restores a few times on Friday the 13th is unfairly
penalised.

Of course, luck isn't all that hard to inflate 'legally' (within the confines
of the game).


